  "body": "The WebUSB specification for the `selectAlternateInterface` function only describes the process of issuing a `SET_INTERFACE` control transfer. However, this functionality is often used for isochronous transfers which have reserved/guaranteed bandwidth on the bus. Because of this, operating systems typically require using a special function to do this (rather than issuing a raw control transfer) so that it can make sure the bus actually has sufficient bandwidth for the new configuration.\n\nHow should failures in this bandwidth allocation process be reported?",
